sequenceDiagram
    actor User as Operator (a laptop)
    participant CS as ConfigSyncSubcommand
    participant CFG as deployment files<br/>(~/.baas/deployments/*.yaml)
    participant STS as AWS STS
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation

    Note over User,CF: baas --deployment <name> config sync [--operator-aws-profile p] -- a laptop adopting a deployment.<br/>CI never syncs: with no file, every command takes the deployment from its operator role.<br/>Never derived: with nothing configured the name is required. With exactly one configured, a bare sync re-verifies it.
    User->>CS: baas --deployment baas-123456789012 config sync --operator-aws-profile my-sso
    CS->>CFG: loadForSync()
    alt no --deployment, and none or 2+ configured
        CS-->>User: name the deployment (the configured ones listed) -- exit 2, nothing written
    end
    Note over CS: the named deployment's file, or a new one -- or the only configured one.<br/>Source: --operator-aws-profile, else aws.operatorProfile, else aws.deployerProfile, else the default chain
    CS->>STS: GetCallerIdentity (source)
    alt the caller is this deployment's operator role
        Note over CS: used as is -- no AssumeRole
    else the caller is another deployment's operator role
        CS-->>User: refused, naming both deployments -- exit 1, nothing written
    else any other caller
        CS->>STS: AssumeRole <name>-role-operator in the caller's account
        alt refused
            CS-->>User: cannot assume the role from that source -- exit 1, nothing written
        end
    end
    CS->>S3: HeadBucket(<name>) as the operator, from AWS_REGION or the default (sync finds the region afresh)
    Note over CS,S3: bucket names are global: a wrong-region request answers 301/400<br/>with x-amz-bucket-region, and a 404 means no bucket
    alt no bucket
        CS-->>User: "No deployment named ... no bucket of that name" -- exit 1, nothing written
    end
    CS->>CF: DescribeStacks(<name>) in the bucket's region, as the operator
    alt stack absent
        CF-->>CS: does not exist
        CS-->>User: a bucket but no stack -- nothing to adopt -- exit 1, nothing written
    else stack present
        CF-->>CS: outputs
        Note over CS: Outputs prove existence only -- nothing is copied.<br/>Names derive from the deployment name, subnet + security group are resolved per job.
        CS->>CFG: save deployments/<name>.yaml -- aws.region, and aws.operatorProfile if given (no name, no defaults)
        CS-->>User: Adopted <name> in <region> -- bucket, table -- exit 0
    end
